From 0014-nouveau-irq-msi-handled Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 26 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 0014/0014] core/intr: IRQ_HANDLED for private MSI line (fix 'Disabling IRQ')

On the MacBookPro11,3 the nonstall fence notify is routed to the separate
NRHOST interrupt line (PMC INTR_NRHOST 0x000104, leaf 1), which has no
registered handler: gk104_mc_intrs[] only lists leaf-0 masks, so a flood
of nonstall notifications (e.g. glmark2 --frame-end none at ~8000 FPS,
7.3M MSI interrupts) makes nvkm_intr() return IRQ_NONE and the kernel's
spurious-interrupt detector disables the IRQ after 100k IRQ_NONE
("irq 91: nobody cared ... Disabling IRQ #91"), leaving the dGPU
unusable until reboot (raport 78).

This is a driver bug, not our 0011-0013 patches: the nonstall path is
consumed via the fifo nonstall event (0x002140), not through a nvkm_inth,
so IRQ_NONE was the intended upstream return for it (Skeggs 2023 treated
it as normal and only added debug-level logging).  The source block
(nvkm_intr_block_locked, INTR_MASK_NRHOST 0x000644) still runs above and
remains as protection; claim the private MSI line as handled so the
spurious-interrupt detector stays out of it.

Signed-off-by: Krzysztof Kowalski <krzysztof7kowalski@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/core/intr.c |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/core/intr.c	2026-08-27 22:15:11.798701344 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/core/intr.c	2026-08-27 22:15:27.279134475 +0200
@@ -225,6 +225,15 @@
 	nvkm_intr_rearm_locked(device);
 done_unlock:
 	spin_unlock(&device->intr.lock);
+	/* Prywatna linia MSI (nonstall fence notify na leaf 1) nie ma
+	 * rejestrowanego handlera — IRQ_NONE karmi spurious-detector
+	 * (po ~100k wyłącza IRQ, "Disabling IRQ").  Blokada źródeł
+	 * (nvkm_intr_block_locked, INTR_MASK_NRHOST 0x000644) wykonała
+	 * się już wcześniej i zostaje — tu tylko uznajemy przerwanie
+	 * za obsłużone.
+	 */
+	if (ret == IRQ_NONE && device->pci && device->pci->msi)
+		ret = IRQ_HANDLED;
 	return ret;
 }
 
